    "chapter_name": "Binomial Theorem",
    "year": "2022",
    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The number of positive integers&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> such that the constant term in the binomial expansion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>12</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>l</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> is an odd integer, is ______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>12</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>12</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>12</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>36</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>For the term to be independent of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;can be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;to be a whole number.</p><p>But for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>12</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;to be in the form of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>l</mi></math></p><p>Only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn></math> satisfies the above relation.</p>"
  }
}